Science is the whisper of the universe,
The quiet question that never sleeps,
The spark in the mind of a curious child,
The promise a bold explorer keeps.

It lives in the fall of an apple from a tree,
In the orbit of planets far away,
In the dance of atoms, unseen yet real,
In the night that turns to day.

Science is the language of the stars,
Written in numbers, logic, and light,
Decoding the age of mountains and seas,
Measuring darkness, defining bright.

It asks not for belief but for wonder,
Not for faith but a reasoned view,
It builds its throne on evidence strong,
Where ideas are tested and born anew.

In microscopes it finds tiny worlds,
In telescopes it chases the vast,
It reads the stories in fossils and genes,
Unlocking secrets of future and past.

Science is the healer’s steady hand,
The vaccine, the cure, the saving art,
The rhythm mapped on a monitor’s line,
The echo of a beating heart.

It is the bridge from dream to design,
From “What if?” to “Here’s how,”
From fire and wheel to silicon chips,
From then and there to here and now.

Yet science is humble at its core,
It knows how much it does not know,
Each answer opens a thousand doors,
Each discovery makes mystery grow.

So here’s to the minds that question “Why?”,
To the souls unafraid to explore,
For science is more than facts and laws —
It is curiosity at its purest core.

It is humanity reaching outward,
With patience, courage, and sight,
Turning confusion into knowledge,
And knowledge into light.